<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>"+" button (CardChrome + VisualHostRoot) + Fluent Dialog host + host-record seed</title>
    <phase>A: Visual Host + Registry + Event</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>010,011</dependencies>
    <blocks>015</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, fluent-ui, visualhost, frontend</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>PCF UI change across two toolbar paths</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-scoped UI addition (a third toolbar icon) with explicit registry + seed contract</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the "+" toolbar icon (AddRegular) between spaarkle and open in CardChrome and the legacy VisualHostRoot toolbar, gated on createWizardEnabled. On click, resolve the wizard via WizardRegistry and open it in a Fluent Dialog seeded with the host record as initialAssociation + lockAssociation=true.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE PCF developer. Fluent v9 + React 18. Follow ADR-021 (dark mode via semantic tokens) + ADR-022.</role>
  <goal>A "+" button appears only when chartDefinition.createWizardEnabled===true, in both CardChrome and VisualHostRoot; clicking resolves + lazy-mounts the wizard in a Fluent Dialog seeded from the host record; unknown key shows a toast.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §5.2, §5.5. Host record entity/id/name come from context.mode.contextInfo. lockAssociation hides step 1 (from task 014).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/CardChrome.tsx
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/VisualHostRoot.tsx
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
      docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md
      src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/CardChrome.tsx
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/VisualHostRoot.tsx
      docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md
      .claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>In CardChrome iconSlots, add a Fluent Button (AddRegular) between spaarkle and open, rendered only when createWizardEnabled.</step>
    <step>Click handler: resolveWizard(createWizardKey, entitylogicalname); if null → toast "No create wizard registered for {key}"; else open Fluent Dialog with the lazy wizard + WizardHostProps (dataService, authenticatedFetch, bffBaseUrl, navigationService, resolveSpeContainerId, tenantId, initialAssociation={host entity,id,name}, lockAssociation=true).</step>
    <step>Mirror the same treatment in VisualHostRoot's legacy toolbar path.</step>
    <step>Dark-mode: use semantic tokens (ADR-021).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit</tools>
  <outputs>Updated CardChrome.tsx + VisualHostRoot.tsx.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>"+" renders only when createWizardEnabled; hidden otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion>Click opens the resolved wizard modally, seeded with the host record; step 1 hidden.</criterion>
    <criterion>Unknown key → toast, no crash.</criterion>
    <criterion>No regression to spaarkle/open buttons; dark mode correct.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Plus button gated by config">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Visual Host visual whose chart-def has createWizardEnabled=Yes</step>
        <step>Verify "+" icon appears between spaarkle and open</step>
        <step>Set createWizardEnabled=No; reload; verify "+" is gone</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Button visibility tracks the config flag; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode</step><step>Verify "+" icon + dialog adapt</step></steps>
      <expected>All colors use semantic tokens (ADR-021)</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
</task>
